{"_v":1,"id":"mamma-mia-2001","cat":"broadway","bd":{"positive":4,"mixed":4,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://www.nytimes.com/2001/10/19/movies/theater-review-mom-had-a-trio-and-a-band-too.html","d":"2001-10-19","q":"\"The choreography is mostly stuff you could try, accident-free, in your own backyard. And the score consists entirely of songs made famous in the disco era by Abba, music that people seldom admit to having danced to, much less sung in their showers."},{"cn":"Anita Gates","o":"The New York Times","s":73,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/theater/mamma-mia-no-longer-inspires-dancing-in-the-aisles.html","d":"2014-08-19","q":"The Broadway production maintains the sweetness, and that’s a joy."},{"cn":"David Cote","o":"Time Out New York","s":58,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"http://www.timeout.com/newyork/theater/mamma-mia-1","q":"As theater, Mamma Mia! is forgettable."},{"cn":"Clive Barnes","o":"New York Post","s":85,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://nypost.com/2001/10/19/abba-dabba-do-lend-mia-an-ear-mamma-is-a-pop-solid-sensation/","d":"2001-10-19","q":"“Mamma Mia!” flies as tuneful as a lark and as smart as a cuckoo."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"http://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/MammaMia01.html","d":"2001-10-19","q":"\"In terms of theatre, Mamma Mia! has little to offer. The book is paper thin, silly...Still, the legions of ABBA fans who attend Mamma Mia! aren't going to care about much of this. They will doubtlessly have a great time and may well walk away proclaiming Mamma Mia! one of the best shows they've ever seen."},{"cn":"Kristen Balzano","o":"Broadway Voice","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"http://bwayvoice.com/mamma-mia/","q":"Personally, I left this theater ready to get my groove on!"},{"cn":"Jenny Lynne","o":"Mydreamcametrue","s":79,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"http://www.mydreamcametrue.com/mammamia.html","q":"Aaron Lazar's performance as Sam Carmichael is exceptionally engaging and wonderfully real."},{"cn":"Don Shewey","o":"Donshewey","s":74,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"http://www.donshewey.com/theater_reviews/mamma_mia_the_women.html","q":"The bristling misogyny of The Women is unsettling, whether it resides in the characters or in the author."}],"au":{"score":81,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"mz":{"s":81,"c":342,"sr":4}}},"tn":[{"yr":56,"cat":"Best Musical","n":null},{"yr":56,"cat":"Best Book of a Musical","n":"Catherine Johnson"},{"yr":56,"cat":"Best Actress in a Musical","n":"Louise Pitre"},{"yr":56,"cat":"Best Featured Actress in a Musical","n":"Judy Kaye"},{"yr":56,"cat":"Best Orchestrations","n":"Benny Andersson"},{"yr":56,"cat":"Best Orchestrations","n":"Björn Ulvaeus"},{"yr":56,"cat":"Best Orchestrations","n":"Martin Koch"}],"cn":{"t":"Critics find this ABBA jukebox musical a guilty pleasure—lightweight on plot but irresistibly fun, delivering infectious joy and nostalgia that wins over audiences despite its theatrical shortcomings.","rc":8},"bo":{"tw":null,"at":{"g":670150538,"p":5979,"a":7876073}},"hi":"/images/shows/mamma-mia-2001/hero.jpg","vs":{"sl":3,"so":4,"co":5,"am":4,"fa":3},"pd":"2001-10-05","ca":[{"n":"Louise Pitre","r":"Donna Sheridan"},{"n":"Judy Kaye","r":"Rosie"},{"n":"David W. Keeley","r":"Sam Carmichael"},{"n":"Joe Machota","r":"Sky"},{"n":"Tina Maddigan","r":"Sophie Sheridan"},{"n":"Ken Marks","r":"Bill Austin"},{"n":"Karen Mason","r":"Tanya"},{"n":"Dean Nolen","r":"Harry Bright"},{"n":"Meredith Akins","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Leslie Alexander","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Stephan Alexander","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Kim-E J. Balmilero","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Robin Baxter","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Tony Carlin","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Bill Carmichael","r":"Father Alexandrios"},{"n":"Tonya Doran","r":"Lisa"},{"n":"Meghann Dreyfuss","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Somer Lee Graham","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Sara Inbar","r":"Ali"},{"n":"Kristin McDonald","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Adam